#
# WHAT IT COVERS: a whole stream, cut to what its video shows, on the phase-step lookahead with
# late moves and the refusal. The game hitched 172 times an hour and stalled for 100 ms or more
# 28 times an hour. The lock's work sits in the first 28 minutes, up to 1700 s: all 7 lock
# releases, each within a second of a hitch or a stall, and 26 of the 33 lookahead moves. The
# worst blend run, 37 presents at 1033.4 s, comes right after two releases 8 presents apart, in
# a burst of 10 hitches and 2 stalls as the screen goes from the inventory through a trader's
# dialog into the trade screen. The dice game follows and hitches once every 4.31 s in two
# stretches, 1439.5 s to 1463.6 s and 1546.0 s to 1567.3 s: 13 hitches of up to 30 ms with no
# stall. The 20 minutes from 1701 s to 2918 s are the calmest: 10 hitches, no stall and 4 moves.
#
# WINDOW. The video pairs with this log at log time = video time + 46.775 s, from the 2626
# marked frames that open it. It runs 3119.9 s with no holes and shows the game from its first
# frame to its last, so the cut is the video's own span, 46.8 s to 3166.7 s. The game had been
# in its 60 fps regime since 9 s and stays in it until 3173 s. Every second inside the cut that
# falls out of the regime is a single hitch second, 6 of them, so nothing was removed from the
# middle.
#
# FIDELITY. The capture ran the policy the tree ships, so the two lines are comparable. The
# replay reads synth 0.4% against 0.4% (0.4% on the dejitter arm, which is how the stream ran),
# worst run 37 against 37 at the same present, runs >= 50 0 against 0 and pull wraps 33 against
# 33. Counted over this window, blends are 706 against 728, repeats 144 against 146, skips 70
# against 70, lock releases 7 against 7 (five at the same presents, two one present apart) and
# lookahead moves 33 against 33: 26 steps seen, 3 cancelled and 10 late in both. 30 moves land
# on the same presents and two are one present apart. The other is at 53.7 s, seven seconds
# into the window: both sides cancelled a step of about 7 ms and then made a late move, the
# replay 26 presents sooner, so it blends 6 presents where the field blended 32. Leaving that
# event out, the replay blends 4 more presents than the field. Each side refused 6 steps, five
# of them the same: the field refused a second step one present after its move at 1244.7 s,
# which the replay never saw, and the replay refused a step at 1657.2 s where the field logged
# none. Neither side moved in either case.
#
# Bounds on the REPLAY (not the field): inequalities, so an improvement passes and only a
# regression fails. Measured on the policy the capture ran.
